{"name":"Anchor Point","hex":"#435d8b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Anchor Point","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Newfoundland, Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Anchor_Point"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anchor Point, Alaska","blocks":[{"text":"Anchor Point is an unincorporated community and census-designated place (CDP) in Kenai Peninsula Borough, in the U.S. state of Alaska. As of the 2020 census, Anchor Point had a population of 2,105. The community is located along the Sterling Highway, part of Alaska State Route 1. Anchor Point is the westernmost point in the North American highway system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Anchorpoint.jpg/330px-Anchorpoint.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anchor_Point%2C_Alaska","wikidata":"Q489206"},{"title":"Anchor Point, Newfoundland and Labrador","blocks":[{"text":"Anchor Point is a town located in St. Barbe Bay, south of Flower's Cove on the west side of the Great Northern Peninsula, in Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada. It was the first English settlement on what is called the 'French Shore' of Newfoundland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/APwide.jpg/330px-APwide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anchor_Point%2C_Newfoundland_and_Labrador","wikidata":"Q2845747"},{"title":"Anchor point","blocks":[{"text":"In audio and recording, what is known colloquially as an anchor point is a center position in a stereo mix reserved for only three or four important tracks. Most modern pop productions are anchored by lead, bass, kick drum, and snare drum. These are usually within a few degrees of center (horizontal) and front in the mix. Exceptions include early stereo recordings using \"stereo-switching\" rather than pan pots) such as the Beatles's \"Strawberry Fields Forever\" and Jimi Hendrix's \"Purple Haze\". Examples of tracks using anchor points include The Breeders's \"Cannonball\", The Cure's \"Catch\", Lady Gaga's \"Just Dance\", Lily Allen's \"The Fear\", Radiohead's \"Airbag\", Squarepusher's \"Star Time 2\", Stone Roses' \"One Love\", and Weezer's \"My Name Is Jonas\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anchor_point","wikidata":"Q4752707"},{"title":"Anchor","blocks":[{"text":"An anchor is a device, normally made of metal, used to secure a vessel to the bed of a body of water to prevent the craft from drifting due to wind or current. The word derives from Latin ancora, which itself comes from the Greek ἄγκυρα."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Kotwica_SS_Pozna%C5%84.JPG/330px-Kotwica_SS_Pozna%C5%84.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anchor","wikidata":"Q168432"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Anchor_Point%2C_Alaska.JPG/500px-Anchor_Point%2C_Alaska.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Anchor_Point%2C_Alaska.JPG/1280px-Anchor_Point%2C_Alaska.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Anchor_Point%2C_Alaska.JPG/500px-Anchor_Point%2C_Alaska.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sign designating North America's most westerly highway point","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnchor_Point%2C_Alaska.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Anchor_Point_boat_launch_cropped.png/500px-Anchor_Point_boat_launch_cropped.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Anchor_Point_boat_launch_cropped.png/500px-Anchor_Point_boat_launch_cropped.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Launching a boat into Cook Inlet at the Anchor River SRA","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnchor_Point_boat_launch_cropped.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/WelcometoAP.jpg/500px-WelcometoAP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/WelcometoAP.jpg/500px-WelcometoAP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Highway welcoming sign","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWelcometoAP.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Amoco_Cadiz_anchor.jpg/500px-Amoco_Cadiz_anchor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Amoco_Cadiz_anchor.jpg/1280px-Amoco_Cadiz_anchor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Amoco_Cadiz_anchor.jpg/500px-Amoco_Cadiz_anchor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anchor of Amoco Cadiz in Portsall, north-west Brittany, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmoco_Cadiz_anchor.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Ankkuri_Kirjurin_k%C3%A4rjess%C3%A4_1.jpg/500px-Ankkuri_Kirjurin_k%C3%A4rjess%C3%A4_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Ankkuri_Kirjurin_k%C3%A4rjess%C3%A4_1.jpg/1280px-Ankkuri_Kirjurin_k%C3%A4rjess%C3%A4_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wiki